2]\n* # Leading the Charge in Rare Disease Research\n  \n  \n  [ Rare Disease Research & Development ][83]\n[Our Mission]\n\n## Our Mission\n\nWe are pioneering new possibilities for the rare disease community.\n\nOur Innovation\n\n## Pushing the Boundaries of Science\n\nOur research and development is fueled by a relentless sense of urgency and an steadfast commitment\nto helping more rare disease patients and their families around the world.\n\nLearn how we are addressing some of today’s most pressing rare disease challenges by investigating\nin new targets, modalities and technologies, with more opportunities for innovation than ever\nbefore.\n\n[ Our Innovation in Rare ][84]\n\n## Featured Stories\n\n[\n[Gianluca-Pirozzi]\n\nThought Leadership • August 19, 2026\n\nAdvancing Rare Disease Research Through Patient-Centric Trial Design: Hear from Alexion R&D leader\nGianluca Pirozzi\n\n][85]\n\nData Science and AI • August 13, 2026\n\n[ AI to shorten the rare disease diagnosis ][86]\n[Seng H. Cheng]\n\nThought Leadership • August 12, 2026\n\n[ Keeping Patients at the Forefront of Rare Disease Innovation: Hear from Alexion R&D leader Seng H.\nCheng ][87]\n[Complement Inhibition]\n\nResearch and Developm"}}, "page_text": "[Skip to main content][1] * [ Contact Us ][2] * [ Investor Relations ][3] * [ Careers ][4] * Global Back to Menu * North America (3) * [Canada (English)][5] * [Canada (French)][6] * [United States][7] * Europe (15) * [Austria][8] * [Belgium][9] * [Denmark][10] * [France][11] * [Germany][12] * [Ireland][13] * [Italy (English)][14] * [Italy (Italian)][15] * [Netherlands][16] * [Norway][17] * [Spain][18] * [Sweden][19] * [Switzerland][20] * [Turkey][21] * [The United Kingdom][22] * Asia Pacific (2) * [Australia][23] * [Japan][24] * [Home][25] * [AstraZeneca][26] * Search [ [Logo] ][27] Search * About Alexion Back to Menu * ## About Alexion * [ About Us ][28] * [ Leadership ][29] * [ Alexion Charitable Foundation ][30] * [ Sustainability ][31] * Our Science Back to Menu ## Our Science Research and Development Back to Our Science * ## Research and Development * [ Our R&D Approach ][32] * [ Rare Disease R&D ][33] * [ Leadership in Complement ][34] * [ Disease Areas ][35] * [ Our Pipeline ][36] * [ Our Medicines ][37] Innovation Back to Our Science * ## Innovation * [ Data Science and AI ][38] * [ Diagnostics ][39] * [ Genomic Medicine ][40] [ All Innovation ][41] * Our Impact in Rare Back to Menu * ## Our Impact in Rare * [ Living with Rare ][42] * [ Health Equity in Rare ][43] * Supporting Patients and Caregivers Back to Menu * ## Supporting Patients and Caregivers * [ Support Services ][44] * [ Clinical Trials ][45] * [ Managed Access ][46] * Partnering Back to Menu * ## Partnering * [ Discovery Partnerships ][47] * [ Externally Sponsored Research ][48] * [ Grants ][49] * [ Business Development ][50] * Media Back to Menu * ## Media * [ Alexion News Centre ][51] * [ Fact Sheets ][52] * [ Articles ][53] * [ View All Media ][54] * [ Press Releases ][55] * [ Contact Us ][56] * [ Investor Relations ][57] * [ Careers ][58] * Global Back to Menu * North America (3) * [Canada (English)][59] * [Canada (French)][60] * [United States][61] * Europe (15) * [Austria][62] * [Belgium][63] * [Denmark][64] * [France][65] * [Germany][66] * [Ireland][67] * [Italy (English)][68] * [Italy (Italian)][69] * [Netherlands][70] * [Norway][71] * [Spain][72] * [Sweden][73] * [Switzerland][74] * [Turkey][75] * [The United Kingdom][76] * Asia Pacific (2) * [Australia][77] * [Japan][78] * [Home][79] * [AstraZeneca][80] * Search * [Rare Disease Day Article] # Pioneering new possibilities for the rare disease community [ Read More ][81] * # More than 400 Million People Live with a Rare Disease [ Living with Rare ][82] * # Leading the Charge in Rare Disease Research [ Rare Disease Research & Development ][83] [Our Mission] ## Our Mission We are pioneering new possibilities for the rare disease community. Our Innovation ## Pushing the Boundaries of Science Our research and development is fueled by a relentless sense of urgency and an steadfast commitment to helping more rare disease patients and their families around the world. Learn how we are addressing some of today’s most pressing rare disease challenges by investigating in new targets, modalities and technologies, with more opportunities for innovation than ever before. [ Our Innovation in Rare ][84] ## Featured Stories [ [Gianluca-Pirozzi] Thought Leadership • August 19, 2026 Advancing Rare Disease Research Through Patient-Centric Trial Design: Hear from Alexion R&D leader Gianluca Pirozzi ][85] Data Science and AI • August 13, 2026 [ AI to shorten the rare disease diagnosis ][86] [Seng H. Cheng] Thought Leadership • August 12, 2026 [ Keeping Patients at the Forefront of Rare Disease Innovation: Hear from Alexion R&D leader Seng H. Cheng ][87] [Complement Inhibition] Research and Development • August 12, 2026 [ Following the Science: The Evolution of Complement Inhibition in Rare Disease ][88] [DNA] Research and Development • July 16, 2026 [ Advancing genomic medicine in rare diseases ][89] [ [Holding Hands] Health Equity • May 21, 2026 ### Understanding treatment impact and addressing disparities in rare disease care Alexion’s leadership in rare disease is driven by the many individuals whose expertise, creativity and tenacity fuel our commitment to advancing innovative science. ][90] [ [Tinas Big Trip] Article • May 11, 2026 ### Tina’s Big Trip Tina’s Big Trip is a heartfelt book that follow two sisters preparing for a journey to Italy as their family navigates the unseen complexities of rare disease. ][91] [ [Rare Disease Day] Article • February 03, 2026 ### Pioneering new possibilities for the rare disease community Rare Disease Day unites communities to drive strategies, funding, diagnosis and treatment, connecting local and global efforts for earlier, equitable care. ][92] [ [View globe from space] Clinical Trials • October 28, 2025 ### Shaping the future of R&D with real world insights into rare disease Studying a rare disease often involves working with fragmented information, much like piecing together scattered pages of different books, each offering part of the story but rarely forming a complete picture. Researchers face this challenge due to small, often underdiagnosed, patient populations and limited understanding of how these diseases progress over time. ][93] [ [Newborn Screening] Diagnostics • September 17, 2025 ### Genomic Innovation to Support Newborn Screening of Rare Diseases Today, while more than 10,000 rare diseases are known, recommended newborn screening panels cover only about 40 core conditions. This gap underscores the need for innovative approaches to expand the reach of newborn screening. ][94] [ [Sarah Rhee] Thought Leadership • June 11, 2025 ### Paving Regulatory Pathways in Rare Disease Many rare disease medicines are often a first of their kind, and a clear roadmap for their development and approval does not exist. Navigating the complex and sometimes unprecedented regulatory environment for rare disease requires innovation, collaboration and a patient-first mindset. ][95] [ Patient Support • February 05, 2025 ### Addressing the Unmet Needs of the Amyloidosis Community We spoke with Cristina Quarta, Executive Medical Director, about a group of rare diseases known as amyloidosis, the medical needs within this community and how her work as a cardiologist shapes her approach to research and development (R&D) for rare cardiac conditions. ][96] [ Patient Support • June 25, 2024 ### Getting to know Chathuri Daluwatte, an Alexion R&D Leading Voice Artificial Intelligence (AI) is rapidly advancing and has the potential to have a transformative impact on clinical research and development (R&D). ][97] [ Patient Support • April 18, 2024 ### Getting to know Sophia Zilber, Associate Director, Statistical Programming The voices and perspectives of patients play an essential role in rare disease research and development (R&D). ][98] [ Patient Support • April 16, 2024 ### Getting to know Banu Sankaran, an Alexion R&D Leading Voice Diagnostics and artificial intelligence (AI) systems are transforming research and development (R&D) in the healthcare industry. ][99] [ Health Equity • February 06, 2024 ### Driving health equity for the rare disease community Collectively, more than 400 million people around the world are living with a rare disease, defined as conditions that affect a small number of people compared to the general population. ][100] [ Clinical Trials • November 07, 2023 ### Understanding & Overcoming the Challenges in Rare Disease Clinical Trials Why is conducting clinical trials for rare diseases difficult? Because studying a rare disease poses unique challenges and requires thinking differently. ][101] View All News Veeva ID: GL/ALL/0071 ## Leaving Our Site You are now going to another site. Continue [ [Logo] ][102] This website is intended for people seeking information on Alexion, AstraZeneca Rare Disease's worldwide business. Veeva ID: GL/ALL/0071 Date of preparation: January 2025 ### About Alexion * [ About Us ][103] * [ Alexion News Centre ][104] * [ Investor Relations ][105] ### Rare Disease Community * [ Living with Rare ][106] * [ Healthy Equity in Rare ][107] * [ Therapy Areas ][108] ### Medical Community * [ Our Science ][109] * [ Partnership Opportunities ][110] * [ Innovation ][111] * [ Pipeline ][112] ### Connect * [ Contact Us ][113] * [ Careers ][114] * [ Legal Statement and Terms of Use ][115] * [ Privacy Notice ][116] * [ Cookie Settings ][117] * [ AstraZeneca ][118] ALEXION and the Alexion logo are registered trademarks of Alexion Pharmaceuticals, Inc. © 2026, Alexion Pharmaceuticals, Inc. All rights reserved. [1]: #main [2]: /contact-us [3]: https://www.astrazeneca.com/investor-relations.html [4]: https://careers.alexion.com/ [5]: /worldwide/canada [6]: /worldwide/canada-french [7]: http://alexion.us [8]: /worldwide/austria [