.pdf [70]: https://secure.ethicspoint.eu/domain/media/pt/gui/112316/index.html [71]: //policy.cookiereports.com/fc71d046-pt-br.html [72]: # [73]: # [74]: # [75]: #", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "AstraZeneca do Brasil — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Brazilian subsidiary of AstraZeneca, with biologic products in its portfolio; owns and markets its products. | Brazilian subsidiary of AstraZeneca, with biologic products in its portfolio. | Brazil | Cotia, Brazil", "role_description": "Brand"}}, "X Score": "75", "Y Score": "77", "Overall Score": "76", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Biotechnology", "Quadrant": "Leaders"}, {"Company": "AstraZeneca UK Limited", "Website": "https://www.astrazeneca.co.uk", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "Cambridge, United Kingdom", "Continent / Geography": "EU(United Kingdom)", "Operational Presence": "United Kingdom", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "UK-based global biopharmaceutical company with a strong presence in biologics, including respiratory and oncology biologics.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "GB", "Region Code": "EU", "Summary": "AstraZeneca UK Limited — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: UK affiliate of AstraZeneca, a global biopharmaceutical company with biologics in respiratory and oncology.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "95", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "astrazeneca.co.uk", "data": {"company": {"name": "astrazeneca.co.uk"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "* [AstraZeneca websites][1]\n* [Global site][2]\n\n* About us\n  * [About us][3]\n  * Our UK sites\n    * [Our UK sites ][4]\n    * [Cambridge ][5]\n  * [AstraZeneca impact in the UK][6]\n* Partnerships\n  * [Partnerships][7]\n  * [UK partnership stories][8]\n  * [Working with patient groups][9]\n  * [Working with UK healthcare professionals][10]\n  * [Working with the NHS][11]\n  * [Working with government and policy makers][12]\n* Our therapy areas\n  * [Our therapy areas][13]\n  * [Oncology][14]\n  * [Cardiovascular, renal and metabolism][15]\n  * [Respiratory and immunology][16]\n  * [Rare disease][17]\n  * [Vaccines and immune therapies][18]\n* [Medicines][19]\n* Media\n  * [Media][20]\n  * [Articles][21]\n  * Press releases\n    * [Press releases ][22]\n    * [Press releases archive][23]\n* [Sustainability][24]\n* [Careers][25]\n* [Donation of Goods and Services][26]\n* [Contact us][27]\n* [AstraZeneca websites][28]\n* [Global site][29]\n* About us\n  * [About us][30]\n  * Our UK sites\n    * [Our UK sites ][31]\n    * [Cambridge ][32]\n  * [AstraZeneca impact in the UK][33]\n* Partnerships\n  * [Partnerships][34]\n  * [UK partnership stories][35]\n  * [Working with patient groups][36]\n  * [Working with UK healthcare professionals][37]\n  * [Working with the NHS][38]\n  * [Working with government and policy makers][39]\n* Our therapy areas\n  * [Our therapy areas][40]\n  * [Oncology][41]\n  * [Cardiovascular, renal and metabolism][42]\n  * [Respiratory and immunology][43]\n  * [Rare disease][44]\n  * [Vaccines and immune therapies][45]\n* [Medicines][46]\n* Media\n  * [Media][47]\n  * [Articles][48]\n  * Press releases\n    * [Press releases ][49]\n    * [Press releases archive][50]\n* [Sustainability][51]\n* [Careers][52]\n* [Donation of Goods and Services][53]\n* [ Contact us][54]\n\nInspired by what science can do\nPowered by purpose\nDelivering life-changing medicines\nCreating enduring value for society\nPrevious Next Pause Play\n1. container1\n2. container2\n3. container3\n4. container4\n\nWe are the UK’s leading Biopharmaceutical company\n\nHow do we create value for the UK?\n\n[Discover][55]\n\n[Discover][56]\n\nWe work in ambitious, purpose-led partnerships\n\n[Find out more][57]\n\n[Find out more][58]\n\nWe strive to transform health outcomes for patients\n\n[Our therapy areas][59]\n\n[Our therapy areas ][60]\n\nAt AstraZeneca UK, we believe in forming ambitious purpose-led partnerships with government, with\nthe NHS and with academia to transform outcomes at the population level and to continue developing\nthe UK as a global life sciences powerhouse.\n\nTom Keith-Roach\nPresident, AstraZeneca UK\n\n[Learn more about Tom Keith-Roach][61]\n\nPioneering science to transform UK healthcare\n\nWe are the leading BioPharmaceutical company in the UK. Across our work in R&D, manufacturing, and\nour commercial business, we are inspired by what science can do and are on a mission to deliver\nlife-changing medicines, transform population health outcomes and ultimately, accelerate the UK as a\nglobal leader in life sciences.\n\n[Icon 1 document - clinical trials information]\n\nSharing clinical trials information\n\nWe publish information about the registration and results of all new and ongoing clinical trials for\nall products in all phases on our dedicated website. For healthcare professionals.\n\n[Visit site][62]\n\n \n\n[Icon 2 form - adverse events reporting]\n\nAdverse events\n\nAdverse events should be reported. Reporting forms and information can be found at\n[www.mhra.gov.uk/yellowcard][63]. Adverse events should also be reported to AstraZeneca on 0800 783\n0033 or via [https://contactazmedical.astrazeneca.com/][64]\n\n[Visit site][65]\n\n \n\nStories from AstraZeneca UK\n\nWorking in partnership towards a carbon-free future in asthma care\n\nLearn how we are collaborating to create a greener NHS and improve asthma outcomes.\n\n[\n\nLearn more\n\n][66]\n\nA brighter future for healthcare\n\nLearn from AstraZeneca UK President Tom Keith-Roach, on how we are collaborating to restore\nhealthcare excellence in the UK.\n\n[\n\nLearn more\n\n][67]\n\nGB-65847 | DOP: April 20"}}, "page_text": "* [AstraZeneca websites][1] * [Global site][2] * About us * [About us][3] * Our UK sites * [Our UK sites ][4] * [Cambridge ][5] * [AstraZeneca impact in the UK][6] * Partnerships * [Partnerships][7] * [UK partnership stories][8] * [Working with patient groups][9] * [Working with UK healthcare professionals][10] * [Working with the NHS][11] * [Working with government and policy makers][12] * Our therapy areas * [Our therapy areas][13] * [Oncology][14] * [Cardiovascular, renal and metabolism][15] * [Respiratory and immunology][16] * [Rare disease][17] * [Vaccines and immune therapies][18] * [Medicines][19] * Media * [Media][20] * [Articles][21] * Press releases * [Press releases ][22] * [Press releases archive][23] * [Sustainability][24] * [Careers][25] * [Donation of Goods and Services][26] * [Contact us][27] * [AstraZeneca websites][28] * [Global site][29] * About us * [About us][30] * Our UK sites * [Our UK sites ][31] * [Cambridge ][32] * [AstraZeneca impact in the UK][33] * Partnerships * [Partnerships][34] * [UK partnership stories][35] * [Working with patient groups][36] * [Working with UK healthcare professionals][37] * [Working with the NHS][38] * [Working with government and policy makers][39] * Our therapy areas * [Our therapy areas][40] * [Oncology][41] * [Cardiovascular, renal and metabolism][42] * [Respiratory and immunology][43] * [Rare disease][44] * [Vaccines and immune therapies][45] * [Medicines][46] * Media * [Media][47] * [Articles][48] * Press releases * [Press releases ][49] * [Press releases archive][50] * [Sustainability][51] * [Careers][52] * [Donation of Goods and Services][53] * [ Contact us][54] Inspired by what science can do Powered by purpose Delivering life-changing medicines Creating enduring value for society Previous Next Pause Play 1. container1 2. container2 3. container3 4. container4 We are the UK’s leading Biopharmaceutical company How do we create value for the UK? [Discover][55] [Discover][56] We work in ambitious, purpose-led partnerships [Find out more][57] [Find out more][58] We strive to transform health outcomes for patients [Our therapy areas][59] [Our therapy areas ][60] At AstraZeneca UK, we believe in forming ambitious purpose-led partnerships with government, with the NHS and with academia to transform outcomes at the population level and to continue developing the UK as a global life sciences powerhouse. Tom Keith-Roach President, AstraZeneca UK [Learn more about Tom Keith-Roach][61] Pioneering science to transform UK healthcare We are the leading BioPharmaceutical company in the UK. Across our work in R&D, manufacturing, and our commercial business, we are inspired by what science can do and are on a mission to deliver life-changing medicines, transform population health outcomes and ultimately, accelerate the UK as a global leader in life sciences. [Icon 1 document - clinical trials information] Sharing clinical trials information We publish information about the registration and results of all new and ongoing clinical trials for all products in all phases on our dedicated website. For healthcare professionals. [Visit site][62] [Icon 2 form - adverse events reporting] Adverse events Adverse events should be reported. Reporting forms and information can be found at [www.mhra.gov.uk/yellowcard][63]. Adverse events should also be reported to AstraZeneca on 0800 783 0033 or via [https://contactazmedical.astrazeneca.com/][64] [Visit site][65] Stories from AstraZeneca UK Working in partnership towards a carbon-free future in asthma care Learn how we are collaborating to create a greener NHS and improve asthma outcomes. [ Learn more ][66] A brighter future for healthcare Learn from AstraZeneca UK President Tom Keith-Roach, on how we are collaborating to restore healthcare excellence in the UK. [ Learn more ][67] GB-65847 | DOP: A