of high value biosimilar programs with a primary focus on\nOncology and Immunology therapeutic segments.\n\n[Slide 5]\n\n# Annual Report\n\nTo access the comprehensive details of our annual performance, please click the link below to view\nour annual report.\n\n[Slide 6]\n\n# Corporate Social Responsibility\n\nAurobindo Pharma Foundation, the philanthropic arm of Aurobindo Pharma Limited, strives to transform\nand uplift the lives of underserved communities.\n\n[Slide 7]\n\n# Crafting a Responsible Tomorrow\n\nAurobindo Pharma commits itself to creating a more equitable and inclusive society by supporting\nprocesses that lead to a sustainable transformation.\n\n[Slide 8]\n\n# Life @ Aurobindo\n\nThe culture at Aurobindo is one of learning, collaboration, inclusivity with unlimited opportunities\nfor our employees\n\nPreviousNext\n\n## A global footprint of excellence\n\n[Footprint"}}, "page_text": "[[Logo][Logo]][1] * [About Us][2] * [About Aurobindo][3] * [Vision / Mission][4] * [Milestones][5] * [R&D][6] * [Manufacturing][7] * [Management][8] * [Board of Directors][9] * [Our Presence][10] * [Our Business][11] * [APUSA ][12] * [Europe][13] * [Growth Markets][14] * [ARV][15] * [Overview][16] * [Key facts about HIV/AIDS][17] * [Products][18] * [Global Partners][19] * [Gallery][20] * [Corporate Video][21] * [Apitoria (API)][22] * [Eugia (Speciality products)][23] * [Curateq (Biosimilars) / Peptide ][24] * [Sustainability][25] * [ESG / Sustainability][26] * [ESG Profile][27] * [Sustainability Reports][28] * [BMW Reports][29] * [Social Accountability Standards][30] * [Social Compliance Certification][31] * [Sustainability of Social Accountability Standards][32] * [Human Rights Policy][33] * [Progressive Health and Safety Practices][34] * [Community Impact][35] * [Supply Chain Management][36] * [Supplier Code of Conduct][37] * [CSR][38] * [Aurobindo Pharma Foundation][39] * [CSR Policy][40] * [Annual Report][41] * [Gallery][42] * [Annual Action Plan][43] * [Impact Assess