ick the link below to view our annual report. [Slide 6] # Corporate Social Responsibility Aurobindo Pharma Foundation, the philanthropic arm of Aurobindo Pharma Limited, strives to transform and uplift the lives of underserved communities. [Slide 7] # Crafting a Responsible Tomorrow Aurobindo Pharma commits itself to creating a more equitable and inclusive society by supporting processes that lead to a sustainable transformation. [Slide 8] # Life @ Aurobindo The culture at Aurobindo is one of learning, collaboration, inclusivity with unlimited opportunities for our employees PreviousNext ## A global footprint of excellence [Footprint] [Footprint] [Footprint] [Footprint] [Footprint] ## Our Key Subsidiaries [[curateq logo]][85] [[Apitoria logo]][86] [[eugia logo]][87] ## Delivering exceptional value to all our consumers worldwide #### [Manufacturing Prowess][88] Our 29 manufacturing facilities across the globe have a manufacturing capacities of 50+ billion formulations units and 19,000+ MT APIs. and have advanced vertical integration to produce finished formulation products at an affordable price. [ Read More >>][89] #### [Global Presence][90] We are present across 150+ global markets including the US, Europe and Growth Markets, and are ranked amongst the top 10*** generic companies across eight countries in Europe. [ Read More >>][91] #### [Research & Development][92] Steadfast in our commitment to innovation & research, we invest significantly in our R&D. 830 filings for ANDAs in the US, with 600+ approvals for the same. [ Read More >>][93] ## News & Updates Loading... ## STAY CONNECTED * Largest generic Pharma Company in the US (by Rx dispensed as per MAT March 2024) ** Global workforce including both permanent employees and contractual workers *** Source: IQVIA data MAT Q3 2024 [[Footer Logo]][94] REGISTERED OFFICE Plot no. 2, Maitrivihar, Ameerpet, Hyderabad-500038, Telangana, India. CORPORATE OFFICE Galaxy, Floors: 22-24, Plot No.1, Survey No.83/1, Hyderabad Kno