Emirates][92] ##### International [Global website][93] [International HQ][94] * Disease Areas * Alzheimer's Disease * Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis * Friedreich Ataxia * Kidney Disease * Lupus * Multiple Sclerosis * Postpartum Depression * Spinal Muscular Atrophy Science & Innovation * R&D Expertise * Pipeline * Clinical Trials * Early Access Programs * Making Medicines Safely & Reliably * Our Scientists Medicines * Report a Side Effect Responsibility * Access and Health Equity * Culture & Inclusion * Environment * The CoLab * Reporting & Principles * [2025 Corporate Responsibility Report][95] Company * Mission and Culture * Our U.S. Legacy * Leadership Team * Board of Directors * Biogen Foundation * Contact Us Careers * Search Jobs * Life at Biogen * How We Hire * Career Categories * Student Programs [Investors][96] [Partners][97] [News][98] Our Experts # Shaping the Future of Lupus Care ## What's new? [See all news][99] Error ### Making Breakthroughs Happen Breakthroughs are more than milestones—they’re moments when hope turns into reality. For decades, Biogen has created medicines for hard-to-treat diseases. Scientific curiosity and aspirations to help people around the world are at the core of our legacy and our vision for the future. [Discover Biogen][100] Science & Innovation ## Driving an Innovative Pipeline We’re using cutting-edge science to develop potential breakthrough therapies in neurology, immunology, and rare diseases. [View Our Pipeline][101] [Petri dish] [Petri dish] [Two Biogen employees in the lab] [Two Biogen employees in the lab] Careers ## Caring Deeply. Achieving Excellence. Changing Lives. We came to Biogen to make an impact, to transform rigorous science into first-in-class medicines. We stay to create new possibilities together. We strive for excellence and go beyond the expected because we care deeply about making a difference for the many people we serve. Our dedication to our work is not just about professional achievement; it is about the profound impact that our work can have. [Search open positions][102] ## Stories [See all Stories][103] [ [Ashley standing outside] ][104] Living with PNH #### Living with PNH: Ashley’s Story [ [Chase] ][105] Living with C3G #### Living with C3G: Chase’s Story [ [Brian Hills] ][106] People & Culture #### Leading at the Intersection of Implantable Device and Biopharma: Meet Brian Hills [See all Stories][107] [ [Image] ][108] Information for * [Medical Professionals ][109] * [Investors ][110] * [Media ][111] * [Job Seekers ][112] Get in touch * [Contact us ][113] * [Biogen International ][114] Explore * [Stories ][115] * [Disease Areas ][116] * [Pipeline ][117] We recommend * [Biogen Foundation ][118] * [Corporate Responsibility Report ][119] * [Reporting and Principles ][120] * [Access & Health Equity ][121] * [Culture & Inclusion ][122] [ [Image] ][123] * Information for * [Medical Professionals ][124] * [Investors ][125] * [Media ][126] * [Job Seekers ][127] Get in touch * [Contact us ][128] * [Biogen International ][129] Explore * [Stories ][130] * [Disease Areas ][131] * [Pipeline ][132] We recommend * [Biogen Foundation ][133] * [Corporate Responsibility Report ][134] * [Reporting and Principles ][135] * [Access & Health Equity ][136] * [Culture & Inclusion ][137] © 2026 Biogen * [ Terms & Conditions ][138] * [ Privacy Center ][139] * [ Consumer Health Data Privacy Policy ][140] * [ Cookie Settings ][141] * [ Forward-looking Statement ][142] * [ Community Guidelines ][143] [ ][144] [ ][145] [ ][146] [ ][147] [ ][148] [1]: /home.html [2]: /home.html [3]: /disease-areas.html [4]: /disease-areas/alzheimers-disease.html [5]: /disease-areas/amyotrophic-lateral-sclerosis.html [6]: /disease-areas/friedreich-ataxia.html [7]: /disease-areas/kidney-disease.html [8]: /disease-areas/lupus.html [9]: /disease-areas/multiple-sclerosis.html [10]: /disease-areas/postpartum-depression.html [11]: /disease-areas/spinal-muscular-atrophy.html [12]: /stories/living-with-lupus-cle-s