y company specializing in neurological biologics; markets products under its brand. | UK affiliate of Biogen, a biotechnology company specializing in neurological biologics. | United Kingdom | Berkshire, United, Kingdom", "role_description": "Brand"}}, "X Score": "43", "Y Score": "46", "Overall Score": "44", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Biotechnology", "Quadrant": "Emerging Players"}, {"Company": "Biolab Sanus Farmacêutica", "Website": "https://www.biolab.com.br", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "São Paulo, Brazil", "Continent / Geography": "LATAM(Brazil)", "Operational Presence": "Brazil", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Develops and markets biosimilars in Brazil, including insulin glargine and others.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "BR", "Region Code": "LATAM", "Summary": "Biolab Sanus Farmacêutica — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Biolab develops and markets biosimilars in Brazil, including insulin glargine, indicating it owns or markets products in this market.", "Data Sources": "google_ai; openai_sdk_residual", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "90", "X Score": "40", "Y Score": "41", "Overall Score": "40", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Biotechnology", "Quadrant": "Emerging Players"}, {"Company": "Biomarin Pharmaceutical", "Website": "https://www.biomarin.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "San, Rafael, California", "Continent / Geography": "NA(United States)", "Operational Presence": "United States", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "BioMarin markets biologic enzyme replacement therapies for rare genetic diseases.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "US", "Region Code": "NA", "Summary": "Biomarin Pharmaceutical — channel participant (chatgpt_recall). Verify: BioMarin markets biologic enzyme replacement therapies for rare genetic diseases, owning and marketing branded biologics.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "95", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "biomarin.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "biomarin.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "[[Biomarin]][1]\n* [Company][2]\n  * [About Us][3]\n  * [Our Origin Story][4]\n  * [Leadership Team][5]\n  * [Board of Directors][6]\n  * [Responsibility][7]\n  * [Giving][8]\n* [Patients][9]\n  * [Patients][10]\n  * [Patient Support][11]\n  * [RARE Scholars][12]\n  * [Expanded Access][13]\n* [Science & Medicine][14]\n  * [Our Science][15]\n  * [Medicines][16]\n  * [Pipeline][17]\n  * [Manufacturing][18]\n  * [Clinical Trials][19]\n  * [Publications][20]\n  * [Medical Information][21]\n  * [External Scientific Support][22]\n* [News][23]\n  * [Newsroom][24]\n  * [Stories][25]\n  * [Press Releases][26]\n  * [Company Statements][27]\n* [Careers][28]\n  * [Careers at BioMarin][29]\n  * [Fellowships][30]\n* [Investors][31]\n* [Locations][32]\n* [Contact][33]\n* [Locations][34]\n* [Contact][35]\n[Search][36]\nSearch BioMarin\n[featured image ben schooler]\n\n## Bringing Science Full Circle: Ben Schooler Shares What Has Motivated His Path at BioMarin\n\nFrom college genetics labs to leading strategy in Technical Operations, Ben Schooler’s career\nreflects a deep respect for science, connection and the patients BioMarin serves. He shares what\ninspires his work – and the perspectives that keep him grounded.\n\n[READ MORE][37]\n\n[Science Photo]\n\n## BioMarin to Acquire Alesta Therapeutics to Gain ALE1, a Potential First Oral Therapy for\n## Hypophosphatasia\n\nThe transaction will add an important clinical program to BioMarin’s pipeline.\n\n[READ MORE][38]\n\n[Cristin Hubbard]\n\n## Cristin Hubbard Reflects on a Career Spent Bringing Innovation to Patients – and Why Working at\n## BioMarin Has Her More Energized Than Ever\n\nOur Chief Commercial Officer discusses her professional journey, her leadership philosophy and how\nher experience across a variety of roles has prepared her for this moment at BioMarin.  \n\n[READ MORE][39]\n\n## Breakthrough Science\n\nWe relentlessly pursue bold science to translate genetic discoveries into new medicines that advance\nthe future of human health.\n\n[Learn More][40]\n\n[Kennedy \"KK\" Davlin]\n\n## Focus on Patients\n\nWe listen to and learn from patient communities to collaborate on solutions with the potential to\nhelp improve care.\n\n[Learn More][41]\n\n[Javier Femenia]\n\n## People-First Culture\n\nOur talented and dedicated people represent the best the biotech industry has to offer and have\nhelped shape a culture focused on working together to deliver for the patients we serve.\n\n[Learn More][42]\n\n## BioMarin is a leading, global rare disease biotechnology company focused on delivering medicines\n## for people living with genetically defined conditions.\n\nFounded in 1997, we have a proven track record of innovation, with nine commercial therapies and a\nstrong clinical and preclinical pipeline. Using a distinctive approach to drug discovery and\ndevelopment, BioMarin seeks to unleash the full potential of genetic science by pursuing\ncategory-defining medicines that have a profound impact on patients.\n\n[Learn More][43]\n\n## Press Releases\n\n### [BioMarin to Acquire Alesta Therapeutics to Gain ALE1, a Potential First Oral Therapy for\n### Hypophosphatasia, Adding an Important Clinical Program to BioMarin’s Pipeline][44]\n\nAugust 18, 2026\n\n### [BioMarin to Participate at the Canaccord Genuity 46th Annual Growth Conference on Wednesday,\n### August 12, 2026, at 8:00AM ET in Boston][45]\n\nAugust 10, 2026\n\n### [BioMarin Reports Second Quarter 2026 Financial and Operating Results][46]\n\nAugust 6, 2026\n\n### [BioMarin to Host Second Quarter 2026 Financial Results Conference Call and Webcast on Thursday,\n### August 6, 2026, at 4:30pm ET][47]\n\nJuly 30, 2026\n\n### [BioMarin and n-Lorem Foundation Enter Early Research Collaboration to Develop Potential\n### First-in-Disease Medicine for Newly Identified ReNU Syndrome][48]\n\nJuly 27, 2026\n\n[More][49]\n\n## News\n\n[[Becky Curran]][50]\n* [Community][51]\n\n### [Becky Jackson Curran Advocates for Accessibility and Understanding][52]\n\nJuly 14, 2026\n\n[[Megan Bull]][53]\n* [People and Culture][54]\n* [Science][55]\n\n### [Megan Bull’s Childhood Empathy Fuels a Career"}}, "page_text": "[[Biomarin]][1] * [Company][2] * [About Us][3] * [Our Origin Story][4] * [Leadership Team][5] * [Board of Directors][6] * [Responsibility][7] * [Giving][8] * [Patients][9] * [Patients][10] * [Patient Support][11] * [RARE Scholars][12] * [Expanded Access][13] * [Science & Medicine][14] * [Our Science][15] * [Medicines][16] * [Pipeline][17] * [Manufacturing][18] * [Clinical Trials][19] * [Publications][20] * [Medical Information][21] * [External Scientific Support][22] * [News][23] * [Newsroom][24] * [Stories][25] * [Press Releases][26] * [Company Statements][27] * [Careers][28] * [Careers at BioMarin][29] * [Fellowships][30] * [Investors][31] * [Locations][32] * [Contact][33] * [Locations][34] * [Contact][35] [Search][36] Search BioMarin [featured image ben schooler] ## Bringing Science Full Circle: Ben Schooler Shares What Has Motivated His Path at BioMarin From college genetics labs to leading strategy in Technical Operations, Ben Schooler’s career reflects a deep respect for science, connection and the patients BioMarin serves. He shares what inspires his work – and the perspectives that keep him grounded. [READ MORE][37] [Science Photo] ## BioMarin to Acquire Alesta Therapeutics to Gain ALE1, a Potential First Oral Therapy for ## Hypophosphatasia The transaction will add an important clinical program to BioMarin’s pipeline. [READ MORE][38] [Cristin Hubbard] ## Cristin Hubbard Reflects on a Career Spent Bringing Innovation to Patients – and Why Working at ## BioMarin Has Her More Energized Than Ever Our Chief Commercial Officer discusses her professional journey, her leadership philosophy and how her experience across a variety of roles has prepared her for this moment at BioMarin. [READ MORE][39] ## Breakthrough Science We relentlessly pursue bold science to translate genetic discoveries into new medicines that advance the future of human health. [Learn More][40] [Kennedy \"KK\" Davlin] ## Focus on Patients We listen to and learn from patient communities to collaborate on solutions with the potential to help improve care. [Learn More][41] [Javier Femenia] ## People-First Culture Our talented and dedicated people represent the best the biotech industry has to offer and have helped shape a culture focused on working together to deliver for the patients we serve. [Learn More][42] ## BioMarin is a leading, global rare disease biotechnology company focused on delivering medicines ## for people living with genetically defined conditions. Founded in 1997, we have a proven track record of innovation, with nine commercial therapies and a strong clinical and preclinical pipeline. Using a distinctive approach to drug discovery and development, BioMarin seeks to unleash the full potential of genetic science by pursuing category-defining medicines that have a profound impact on patients. [Learn More][43] ## Press Releases ### [BioMarin to Acquire Alesta Therapeutics to Gain ALE1, a Potential First Oral Therapy for ### Hypophosphatasia, Adding an Important Clinical Program to BioMarin’s Pipeline][44] August 18, 2026 ### [BioMarin to Participate at the Canaccord Genuity 46th Annual Growth Conference on Wednesday, ### August 12, 2026, at 8:00AM ET in Boston][45] August 10, 2026 ### [BioMarin Reports Second Quarter 2026 Financial and Operating Results][46] August 6, 2026 ### [BioMarin to Host Second Quarter 2026 Financial Results Conference Call and Webcast on Thursday, ### August 6, 2026, at 4:30pm ET][47] July 30, 2026 ### [BioMarin and n-Lorem Foundation Enter Early Research Collaboration to Develop Potential ### First-in-Disease Medicine for Newly Identified ReNU Syndrome][48] July 27, 2026 [More][49] ## News [[Becky Curran]][50] * [Community][51] ### [Becky Jackson Curran Advocates for Accessibility and Understanding][52] July 14, 2026 [[Megan Bull]][53] * [People and Culture][54] * [Science][55] ### [Megan Bull’s Childhood Empathy Fuels a Career of Impact][56] July 23, 2026 [[Londyn and Connor Episode 3]][57] * [Community][58] ### [Why Do I Pheel This Way? Episode 3: Finding Strength Through Sports While Living with ### Phenylketonuria][59] June 25, 2026 [[Carissah and Angela]][60] * [Community][61] ### [Crossing Paths: How the National MPS Society Reaches Families Where They Are][62] May 13, 2026 ## Social * [LinkedIn][63] * [X][64] * [Instagram][65] * [Facebook][66] ## Join Our Team Come work with us. Search our global career opportunities to learn how you can make your mark. [Explore Opportunities][67] # You’re leaving the BioMarin website. Links to sites outside of this website are provided as a resource to the viewer. BioMarin accepts no responsibility for the content of linked sites. [Leave this website][68] [Close][69] # Enter your DIN number Please locate the 8-digit DIN number found on your product package or educational materials and enter it in the form below to access important safety information. DIN number [[Biomarin]][70] ###### Contact * [Publication Data Request]