ot publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "German biotech company known for mRNA vaccines and therapeutic biologics.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "DE", "Region Code": "EU", "Summary": "BioNTech SE — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: BioNTech is a biotech company that develops and markets mRNA vaccines and therapeutic biologics; it owns and markets its products.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "90", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "biontech.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "biontech.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "### Sorry. You can not access the page.\n\nThe page pro.biontech.com is not accessible from your location. You have been redirected to our\ncorporate website for more information and resources.\n\n[\nClose ][1]\n* [ Investors ][2]\n* [ Media ][3]\n* [ Healthcare professionals ][4]\n* [ Clinical trials ][5]\n[ Global | EN ][6]\n* [Australia | EN][7]\n* [Deutschland | DE][8]\n* [United States | EN][9]\n[ About ][10] [ Research & innovation ][11] [ Pipeline & products ][12] [ Careers ][13] [ Contact\n][14] [\n][15] [\n][16]\n\n* [ Investors ][17]\n* [ Media ][18]\n* [ Healthcare professionals ][19]\n* [ Clinical trials ][20]\n\n[ Global | EN ][21]\n* [Australia | EN][22]\n* [Deutschland | DE][23]\n* [United States | EN][24]\n\n### We are a global immunotherapy powerhouse aspiring to translate science into survival\n\n[ Read more\n][25]\n1. Home\n\n# Our mission\n\nWe are committed to improving the health of people worldwide with our fundamental research and\ndevelopment of immunotherapies and mRNA vaccines. We believe in scientific rigor, innovation and\npassion as a driving force. BioNTech was founded by scientists and physicians to translate science\ninto survival by combining fundamental research and operational excellence.\n\n[ Read more\n][26]\n\n## Therapeutic areas & priority programs\n\n#### Oncology\n\nWe have built a unique oncology portfolio consisting of three complementary therapeutic modalities:\n**mRNA cancer immunotherapies, next-generation immunomodulators, and targeted therapies**. We\nbelieve that each of these modalities has the potential to offer precise mechanisms for targeting\ncancer cells.\n\n\nAnd we want to go further: We continue to execute our **combination strategy**, aiming to develop\n**new therapies based on synergistic modalities**, ultimately creating space for curative\napproaches. We have identified priority programs to achieve our aim of addressing the full continuum\nof cancer – from resected cancers in the adjuvant setting to later-stage advanced and metastatic\ncancers. \n\n[bnt-home-BNT327_still-render.jpg]\n\n### Our next-generation immunomodulator BNT327\n\nWe believe that this **bispecific antibody candidate** has the potential to become a next-generation\nimmuno-oncology backbone suitable for a broad range of cancers.** **BNT327 binds to both PD-L1 and\nVEGF-A and thus acts on two validated biological mechanisms against cancer in a synergistic manner.\nAdditionally, BNT327’s binding directly positions the therapy candidate where it is needed: in the\ntumor microenvironment.\n\n[ Learn more\n][27]\n\n### Our mRNA cancer immunotherapies\n\nOur **mRNA cancer immunotherapy **approach aims at inducing immune responses against cancer targets\nthat are either individual for each patient or shared by patients with the same tumor type. We\nbelieve that our individualized mRNA cancer immunotherapy candidates are particularly suited for\nearly intervention in the adjuvant setting, after surgery or chemotherapy, where they can address\nresidual tumor cells and potentially prevent disease recurrence.\n\n[ Learn more\n][28]\n\n#### Infectious diseases\n\nWe believe the technology behind our COVID-19 vaccine has potential against a range of other\ninfectious diseases. Our COVID-19 vaccine efforts have demonstrated several advantages over the\ntraditional vaccine development that we aim to translate into new mRNA vaccine programs targeting\ninfectious diseases with a massive health burden.\n\n[ Learn more\n][29]\n\n## Pipeline\n\nWe strive to exploit the full potential of the body’s immune system by combining powerful new\ntherapeutic modalities and a diverse array of biological targets to successfully help address\ncancer, infectious diseases and other serious diseases. \n\n10\n\n+\n\nNovel-novel combination trials\n\n[ Explore more\n][30]\n\n2.1\n\nbn € \n\nInvestment into R&D in 2025 to address cancer care\n\n[ Explore more\n][31]\n\n25\n\n+\n\nPhase 2 and phase 3 clinical trials in oncology\n\n[ Explore more\n][32]\n[BNT_Home_JoinUs_Teaser]\n\n## Join us and become part of our team!\n\nWe are always on the lookout for dedicat"}}, "page_text": "### Sorry. You can not access the page. The page pro.biontech.com is not accessible from your location. You have been redirected to our corporate website for more information and resources. [ Close ][1] * [ Investors ][2] * [ Media ][3] * [ Healthcare professionals ][4] * [ Clinical trials ][5] [ Global | EN ][6] * [Australia | EN][7] * [Deutschland | DE][8] * [United States | EN][9] [ About ][10] [ Research & innovation ][11] [ Pipeline & products ][12] [ Careers ][13] [ Contact ][14] [ ][15] [ ][16] * [ Investors ][17] * [ Media ][18] * [ Healthcare professionals ][19] * [ Clinical trials ][20] [ Global | EN ][21] * [Australia | EN][22] * [Deutschland | DE][23] * [United States | EN][24] ### We are a global immunotherapy powerhouse aspiring to translate science into survival [ Read more ][25] 1. Home # Our mission We are committed to improving the health of people worldwide with our fundamental research and development of immunotherapies and mRNA vaccines. We believe in scientific rigor, innovation and passion as a driving force. BioNTech was founded by scientists and physicians to translate science into survival by combining fundamental research and operational excellence. [ Read more ][26] ## Therapeutic areas & priority programs #### Oncology We have built a unique oncology portfolio consisting of three complementary therapeutic modalities: **mRNA cancer immunotherapies, next-generation immunomodulators, and targeted therapies**. We believe that each of these modalities has the potential to offer precise mechanisms for targeting cancer cells. And we want to go further: We continue to execute our **combination strategy**, aiming to develop **new therapies based on synergistic modalities**, ultimately creating space for curative approaches. We have identified priority programs to achieve our aim of addressing the full continuum of cancer – from resected cancers in the adjuvant setting to later-stage advanced and metastatic cancers. [bnt-home-BNT327_still-render.jpg] ### Our next-generation immunomodulator BNT327 We believe that this **bispecific antibody candidate** has the potential to become a next-generation immuno-oncology backbone suitable for a broad range of cancers.** **BNT327 binds to both PD-L1 and VEGF-A and thus acts on two validated biological mechanisms against cancer in a synergistic manner. Additionally, BNT327’s binding directly positions the therapy candidate where it is needed: in the tumor microenvironment. [ Learn more ][27] ### Our mRNA cancer immunotherapies Our **mRNA cancer immunotherapy **approach aims at inducing immune responses against cancer targets that are either individual for each patient or shared by patients with the same tumor type. We believe that our individualized mRNA cancer immunotherapy candidates are particularly suited for early intervention in the adjuvant setting, after surgery or chemotherapy, where they can address residual tumor cells and potentially prevent disease recurrence. [ Learn more ][28] #### Infectious diseases We believe the technology behind our COVID-19 vaccine has potential against a range of other infectious diseases. Our COVID-19 vaccine efforts have demonstrated several advantages over the traditional vaccine development that we aim to translate into new mRNA vaccine programs targeting infectious diseases with a massive health burden. [ Learn more ][29] ## Pipeline We strive to exploit the full potential of the body’s immune system by combining powerful new therapeutic modalities and a diverse array of biological targets to successfully help address cancer, infectious diseases and other serious diseases. 10 + Novel-novel combination trials [ Explore more ][30] 2.1 bn € Investment into R&D in 2025 to address cancer care [ Explore more ][31] 25 + Phase 2 and phase 3 clinical trials in oncology [ Explore more ][32] [BNT_Home_JoinUs_Teaser] ## Join us and become part of our team! We are always on the lookout for dedicated and curious new talents supporting our team of visionaries. Join us and be part of our unique pioneering spirit. [ Browse our open positions ][33] ### Connect with us Questions about our products, services or clinical trials? Find the right contact person at our Service Center. [ Reach out ][34] ### Stay up to date Looking for latest news, events or SEC filings? Sign-up for our alerts here. [ Subscribe ][35] ### Scientific publications We continue to drive future innovation through sharing key findings in a peer reviewed format. [ Discover ][36] [ About ][37] [ Research & innovation ][38] [ Pipeline ][39] [ Careers ][40] [ Media ][41] [ Investors ][42] [ Healthcare professionals ][43] [ Suppliers ][44] [ Contact ][45] BioNTech SE An der Goldgrube 12 55131 Mainz, Germany T: [+49 6131 9084-0][46] F: +49 6131 9084-2121 M: [service@biontech.de][47] [ Terms of use ][48] [ General conditions of purchase ][49] [ Data privacy statement ][50] [ Adverse event reporting ][51] [ Report a concern ][52] [ Imprint ][53] [ Cookie statement ][54] Cookie settings © 2026 BioNTech SE. All rights reserved. [1]: # [2]: https://investors.biontech.de/ [3]: https://www.biontech.com/int/en/home/media.html [4]: https://pro.biontech.com/de/en/public.html [5]: https://clinicaltrials.biontech.com/ [6]: # [7]: /au/en/home.html [8]: /de/de/home.html [9]: /us/en/home.html [10]: /int/en/home/about.html [11]: /int/en/home/research-and-innovation.html [12]: /int/en/home/pipeline-and-products.html [13]: /int/en/home/careers.html [14]: /int/en/home/contact.html [15]: # [16]: # [17]: https://investors.biontech.de/ [18]: https://www.biontech.com/int/en/home/media.html [19]: https://pro.biontech.com/de/en/public.html [20]: https://clinicaltrials.biontech.com/ [21]: # [22]: /au/en/home.html [23]: /de/de/home.html [24]: /us/en/home.html [25]: /int/en/home/about/vision-and-mission.html [26]: /int/en/home/about/vision-and-mission.html [27]: /int/en/home/pipeline-and-products/pipeline.html#pumitamig [28]: /int/en/home/pipeline-and-products/pipeline.html?search=mRNA&TherapeuticArea=Oncology#pipeline [29]: /int/en/home/research-and-innovation/therapeutic-areas/infectious-diseases.html [30]: /int/en/home/pipeline-and-products/pipeline.html?combination=combinationInclude#pipeline [31]: /int/en/home/pipeline-and-products/pipeline.html#pipeline [32]: /int/en/home/pipeline-and-products/pipeline.html?phase=phase2&phase=phase2-3&phase=phase3#pipe line [33]: https://jobs.biontech.com/ [34]: /int/en/home/contact.html [35]: https://investors.biontech.de/ir-resources/investor-alerts [36]: /int/en/home/research-and-innovation/publications.html [37]: /int/en/home/about.html [38]: /int/en/home/research-and-innovation.html [39]: /int/en/home/pipeline-and-products/pipeline.html [40]: /int/en/home/careers.html [41]: /int/en/home/mediaroom.html [42]: https://investors.biontech.de/ [43]: /int/en/home/hcp-hub.html [44]: /int/en/home/supplier.html [45]: /int/en/home/contact.html [46]: tel:004961319084 [47]: