d Yervoy, significant in oncology biologics.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "", "Region Code": "", "Summary": "Bristol-Myers Squibb — channel participant (chatgpt_recall). Verify: BMS markets biologic drugs such as Opdivo and Yervoy.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "95", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "bms.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "bms.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "[Skip to Main Content][1]\n[ [Bristol Myers Squibb Logo] ][2]\n* [ Contact Us ][3]\n* [ Investors ][4]\n* [ Careers ][5]\n* United States\nBack\n[ [Bristol Myers Squibb Logo] ][6]\n* Science\n  Back\n  [ [Science Firsthand: Making the leap to intentionally designed degraders ]\n  \n  Science Firsthand: Making the leap to intentionally designed degraders\n  \n  ][7] [ [Alt]\n  \n  How we orchestrate clinical trials to deliver hope for patients\n  \n  ][8]\n  \n  ## [ Our science ][9]\n  * [ Areas of focus ][10]\n  * [ Science in action ][11]\n  * [ Scientific resources & fact sheets ][12]\n  * [ Technologies ][13]\n  \n  ## [ Research & development ][14]\n  * [ Clinical trials & research ][15]\n  * [ Independent research ][16]\n  * [ Patient safety ][17]\n  * [ Pipeline ][18]\n* Medicine\n  Back\n  [ [fishing]\n  \n  Product Development: Designing patient‑driven therapies for real life\n  \n  ][19] [ [Image Alt text]\n  \n  Understanding behavioral symptoms in Alzheimer’s: Support for care partners\n  \n  ][20]\n  \n  ## [ Medicines ][21]\n  * [ All medicines ][22]\n  * [ Medical information online ][23]\n  * [ Help paying for your medicine ][24]\n  * [ Investigational medicine access ][25]\n  \n  ## [ Medical resources ][26]\n  * [ Resources by therapeutic area ][27]\n  * [ Disease state resources ][28]\n  * [ Resources for healthcare providers ][29]\n* Impact\n  Back\n  [ [building roof top with energy grids]\n  \n  Building a more resilient energy future to support patients\n  \n  ][30] [ [children in africa]\n  \n  Bringing life-saving medicines to more patients: Our commitment to low- and middle-income\n  countries\n  \n  ][31]\n  \n  ## [ Our impact ][32]\n  * [ Patient advocacy ][33]\n  * [ The Bristol Myers Squibb Foundation ][34]\n  * [ Corporate giving ][35]\n  * [ Economic responsibility ][36]\n  * [ Social progress ][37]\n  * [ Environmental sustainability ][38]\n  * [ Population health ][39]\n  \n  ## [ Life + science stories ][40]\n* News\n  Back\n  [ [patients with purpose promo]\n  \n  Patients and purpose in action\n  \n  ][41] [ [Illustration model of protein degradation]\n  \n  Accelerating protein degradation science with AI and machine learning\n  \n  ][42]\n  \n  ## [ Company news ][43]\n  * [ All press releases ][44]\n  * [ Media contacts ][45]\n  \n  ## [ Investors ][46]\n  * [ Stock information ][47]\n  * [ Financial reporting ][48]\n  * [ Analyst coverage ][49]\n  * [ Events & presentations ][50]\n  * [ Shareholder services ][51]\n  * [ Investor contacts ][52]\n* About us\n  Back\n  [ [Toni swinging a golf club against a blue sky]\n  \n  Toni’s story\n  \n  ][53] [ [Japan BMS employees on the bikes]\n  \n  Bristol Myers Squibb employees cycle across four continents to advance cancer research\n  \n  ][54]\n  \n  ## [ Our company ][55]\n  * [ Leadership ][56]\n  * [ Governance ][57]\n  * [ Locations ][58]\n  * [ Partnerships & business development ][59]\n  * [ Working at BMS ][60]\n  \n  ## [ Our commitments ][61]\n  * [ Global inclusion ][62]\n  * [ Transparency & reporting ][63]\n  * [ Positions on key issues ][64]\n* Search\nSearch\n* [ Search Jobs ][65]\n* [ Search U.S. Medical Information ][66]\n\n# World-class science. Life-changing impact.\n\nGet an inside look at the work we do every day to define what's possible and transform patients'\nlives through science.\n\n[ see what drives us ][67]\n\n## The arrival of a new treatment class: First CELMoD approved for patients with multiple myeloma\n\nThe FDA has granted accelerated approval to our multiple myeloma treatment, bringing the first\nCELMoD-based regimen to patients as early as first relapse.\n[ Learn more ][68]\n\n## Life + Science\n\n[ view more stories ][69]\n\n## Areas of focus\n* [\n  \n  ### Oncology\n  \n  Building on our heritage in the treatment of solid tumors, we’re solving complex scientific\n  problems for cancer patients everywhere.\n  \n  Learn more about Oncology ][70]\n* [\n  \n  ### Hematology\n  \n  Known for delivering many transformational firsts in hematology, we’re committed to breaking new\n  ground across diseases with high unmet need.\n  \n  Learn more about Hematology ][71]\n"}}, "page_text": "[Skip to Main Content][1] [ [Bristol Myers Squibb Logo] ][2] * [ Contact Us ][3] * [ Investors ][4] * [ Careers ][5] * United States Back [ [Bristol Myers Squibb Logo] ][6] * Science Back [ [Science Firsthand: Making the leap to intentionally designed degraders ] Science Firsthand: Making the leap to intentionally designed degraders ][7] [ [Alt] How we orchestrate clinical trials to deliver hope for patients ][8] ## [ Our science ][9] * [ Areas of focus ][10] * [ Science in action ][11] * [ Scientific resources & fact sheets ][12] * [ Technologies ][13] ## [ Research & development ][14] * [ Clinical trials & research ][15] * [ Independent research ][16] * [ Patient safety ][17] * [ Pipeline ][18] * Medicine Back [ [fishing] Product Development: Designing patient‑driven therapies for real life ][19] [ [Image Alt text] Understanding behavioral symptoms in Alzheimer’s: Support for care partners ][20] ## [ Medicines ][21] * [ All medicines ][22] * [ Medical information online ][23] * [ Help paying for your medicine ][24] * [ Investigational medicine access ][25] ## [ Medical resources ][26] * [ Resources by therapeutic area ][27] * [ Disease state resources ][28] * [ Resources for healthcare providers ][29] * Impact Back [ [building roof top with energy grids] Building a more resilient energy future to support patients ][30] [ [children in africa] Bringing life-saving medicines to more patients: Our commitment to low- and middle-income countries ][31] ## [ Our impact ][32] * [ Patient advocacy ][33] * [ The Bristol Myers Squibb Foundation ][34] * [ Corporate giving ][35] * [ Economic responsibility ][36] * [ Social progress ][37] * [ Environmental sustainability ][38] * [ Population health ][39] ## [ Life + science stories ][40] * News Back [ [patients with purpose promo] Patients and purpose in action ][41] [ [Illustration model of protein degradation] Accelerating protein degradation science with AI and machine learning ][42] ## [ Company news ][43] * [ All press releases ][44] * [ Media contacts ][45] ## [ Investors ][46] * [ Stock information ][47] * [ Financial reporting ][48] * [ Analyst coverage ][49] * [ Events & presentations ][50] * [ Shareholder services ][51] * [ Investor contacts ][52] * About us Back [ [Toni swinging a golf club against a blue sky] Toni’s story ][53] [ [Japan BMS employees on the bikes] Bristol Myers Squibb employees cycle across four continents to advance cancer research ][54] ## [ Our company ][55] * [ Leadership ][56] * [ Governance ][57] * [ Locations ][58] * [ Partnerships & business development ][59] * [ Working at BMS ][60] ## [ Our commitments ][61] * [ Global inclusion ][62] * [ Transparency & reporting ][63] * [ Positions on key issues ][64] * Search Search * [ Search Jobs ][65] * [ Search U.S. Medical Information ][66] # World-class science. Life-changing impact. Get an inside look at the work we do every day to define what's possible and transform patients' lives through science. [ see what drives us ][67] ## The arrival of a new treatment class: First CELMoD approved for patients with multiple myeloma The FDA has granted accelerated approval to our multiple myeloma treatment, bringing the first CELMoD-based regimen to patients as early as first relapse. [ Learn more ][68] ## Life + Science [ view more stories ][69] ## Areas of focus * [ ### Oncology Building on our heritage in the treatment of solid tumors, we’re solving complex scientific problems for cancer patients everywhere. Learn more about Oncology ][70] * [ ### Hematology Known for delivering many transformational firsts in hematology, we’re committed to breaking new ground across diseases with high unmet need. Learn more about Hematology ][71] * [ ### Neuroscience We’re dedicated to championing the needs and experiences of people living with neurological and psychiatric diseases through disease-modifying and symptomatic therapies. Learn more about neuroscience ][72] * [ ### Immunology We’re working to deliver meaningful solutions that address unmet needs in dermatology, gastroenterology, pulmonology and rheumatology. Learn more about immunology ][73] * [ ### Cardiovascular Building on a 70-year legacy of paradigm-changing medicines, we’re leveraging our experience and expertise to take cardiovascular research to the next level. Learn more about cardiovascular ][74] [ View more ][75] ## Pipeline AS OF JULY 30, 2026 * 49 Compounds in development * 40+ Disease areas being studied Our pipeline targets areas where we can deliver transformative medicines — for patients who need them most. [ EXPLORE THE PIPELINE ][76] ## Latest press releases [ VIEW ALL PRESS RELEASES ][77] ## Navigation * [ Our science ][78] * [ Research & development ][79] * [ Medicines ][80] * [ Medical resources ][81] * [ Our impact ][82] * [ Life & science ][83] * [ Company news ][84] * [ Investors ][85] * [ Our company ][86] * [ Our commitments ][87] ## Resources * [ Legal notice ][88] * [ Privacy notice center ][89] * [ Your privacy choices ][90] * [ Trademarks ][91] * [ Forward-looking statement ][92] * [ Modern slavery statement 