areers ][145] * [A career in data][146] * [Life at GSK][147] * [Outstanding people][148] * [Outstanding people ][149] * [Great place to work][150] * [Meet our veterans][151] * [Working together][152] * [My GSK story][153] * [Innovating together][154] * [Experienced professionals][155] * [Experienced professionals ][156] * [Business operations][157] * [Engineering at GSK ][158] * [Global supply chain][159] * [Sales and marketing][160] * [Research and development][161] * [Research and development ][162] * [Chemical Manufacturing and Controls (CMC), Medicine Development and Supply (MDS)][163] * [Genomic sciences][164] * [Technology][165] * [Early careers][166] * [Early careers ][167] * [Application process][168] * [Apprentice programmes][169] * [Internships and placements][170] * [Graduate programme][171] * [Graduate programme ][172] * [Business operations][173] * [Engineering][174] * [Manufacturing & supply][175] * [Commercial ][176] * [Research & development][177] * [Manufacturing sciences & technology][178] * [Post graduate opportunities][179] * [Frequently asked questions][180] * [Veterans][181] * [Our global and regional hubs][182] * [How we hire][183] * [How we hire ][184] * [Fraudulent internet recruitment activities][185] * [Frequently asked questions][186] * [Dark mode][187] Switch to dark mode to head towards a more sustainable world together. [More info][188] * [[Healthcare professionals] Healthcare professionals][189] * [[Contact us] Contact us][190] [GSK Homepage][191] Search[Menu][192] Submit form * Global * [Change location][193] * [Dark mode][194] Switch to dark mode to head towards a more sustainable world together. [More info][195] * [[Healthcare professionals] Healthcare professionals][196] * [[Contact us] Contact us][197] * Search [GSK Homepage][198] * [Behind the Science magazine][199] * [Company][200] * [Innovation][201] * [Products][202] * [Responsibility][203] * [Investors][204] * [Media][205] * [Careers][206] # Behind the science ## ‘It’s always there’: Living with the burden of chronic hepatitis B Hepatitis B is a viral liver infection affecting hundreds of millions of people worldwide. Chronic infections increase the risk of developing liver cancer or cirrhosis, particularly if left untreated. Mother of two Natalia shares her journey from diagnosis to treatment, and the constant worries she has while raising a family. [Read Natalia’s story][207] [Natalia carrying her daughter with her husband and other daughter walking in the background] [Close video][208] ## Who we are As a focused biopharma company, we discover, develop and deliver medicines and vaccines to create value for patients and shareholders. We aim to positively impact the health of 2.5 billion people by the end of the decade. Our R&D focus is on four therapeutic areas: respiratory, immunology and inflammation; oncology; HIV; and infectious diseases. [Purpose, strategy and culture][209] [Why invest in GSK?][210] Respiratory, immunology and inflammation 7m deaths each year due to lung diseases [Go to respiratory, immunology and inflammation][211] Oncology ~10m people die from cancer each year [Go to oncology][212] HIV 40m people living with HIV globally [Go to HIV][213] Infectious diseases 1 in 7 deaths globally caused by infectious disease [Go to infectious diseases][214] previousnext Behind the Science ## Exploring how today's discoveries are shaping tomorrow's health [ ### 'I had dreams': How HIV care has evolved across a generation ][215] [ ### 'Long-acting options are the future to prevent transmission of HIV' ][216] [ ### ‘It’s always there’: Learning to live with chronic hepatitis B ][217] [ ### ‘The roar I hear is the next stage of the rocket firing’: MAPS technology and the new age of ### vaccine development ][218] [ ### Antibody-drug conjugates: Advancing the search for more targeted cancer treatment ][219] [ ### Mapping disease at the cellular level: A single-cell revolution in drug discovery ][220] [ ### Why adults aged 50 years and older with certain long-term health conditions need to make their ### move to help protect against this common respiratory virus ][221] [ ### 'The ever-present threat of contracting a UTI means my daily routine is ruled by measures to ### reduce my risk' ][222] [ ### 'We’re innovating to help keep COPD patients out of hospital and exacerbation-free' ][223] [ ### 'Prevention is the best medicine to stop disease before it starts' ][224] previousnext [Read our magazine][225] ### INVESTORS We announced our second quarter 2026 results on Tuesday 28 July [View latest results][226] [Continue to Company ][227] [Gsk Logo][228] This is our global website, intended for visitors seeking information on GSK's worldwide business. Our market sites can be reached by visiting our [location selector. ][229] © 2001-2026 GSK plc. All rights reserved. Trade marks are owned by or licensed to the GSK group of companies. GSK plc. Registered in England and Wales No. 3888792. Registered office: 79 New Oxford Street, London. United Kingdom. WC1A 1DG [ > Modern Slavery Act Statement 2025 (PDF - 187.7KB)][230] GSK websites * [Locations selector][231] * [Social media directory][232] * [GSKPro for healthcare professionals][233] * [GSK study register][234] * [Supplier website][235] * [ViiV Healthcare][236] Quick links * [Behind the Science magazine][237] * [Company][238] * [Innovation][239] * [Products][240] * [Responsibility][241] * [Investors][242] * [Media][243] * [Careers][244] Get in touch * [Contact us][245] * [Partnerships][246] * [Report a possible side effect][247] * [GSK Speak up][248] Follow us on: * [Accessibility][249] * [Digital sustainability][250] * [Terms of use][251] * [Cookie policy][252] * [Privacy notice][253] * [Sitemap][254] [1]: #main-content [2]: #header-search [3]: /en-gb/behind-the-science-magazine/ [4]: /en-gb/company/ [5]: /en-gb/company/ [6]: /en-gb/company/purpose-strategy-and-culture/ [7]: /en-gb/company/gsk-at-a-glance/ [8]: /en-gb/company/history-and-heritage/ [9