ents and presentations, news, stock information and investor contacts.\n\n### Sustainability\n\nWe operate responsibly every day to enable a safe and healthy future for people and communities\nglobally.\n\n## Explore our stories\n\n[ ][82]\n[\nInnovation\nWhat are individualized neoantigen therapies? ][83]\n[ ][84]\n[ Health awareness\nUnderstanding melanoma: The signs and risk factors\n][85]\n[ ][86]\n[ Innovation\nHow Merck scientists are driving next-generation cancer research\n][87]\n[ ][88]\n[ Innovation\nMerck’s One Pipeline strategy: Purpose, patients and big bets on science\n][89]\n1\n\n[Read more stories][90]\n\n### About us\n\nFor more than 130 years, we have brought hope to humanity through the development of important\nmedicines and vaccines. \n\n[Who we are][91]\n[What we do][92]\n×\n\n### Pipeline\n\nWe follow the science where we can make the greatest difference, now and in the future.\n\n[Explore our pipeline][93]\n×\n\n### Clinical trials\n\nClinical trials help find new treatments to help save and improve lives. Our progress is due in\nlarge part to the important and tough scientific questions we set out to answer with our"}}, "page_text": "[Skip to content][1] [ [Site logo] ][2] Search everything Close Menu Close [Main menu][3] * [Company][4] * [Who we are][5] * [What we do][6] * [Stories][7] * [History][8] * [Sustainability][9] * [Sustainability overview][10] * [Philanthropy][11] * [Merck Medical Outreach Program][12] * [Impact Venture Fund][13] * [Transparency disclosures][14] * [Sustainability resources][15] * [Leadership][16] * [Leadership overview][17] * [Board of directors][18] * [Executive team][19] * [Culture & values][20] * [Culture & values overview][21] * [Code of conduct, ethics & compliance][22] * [Diversity and inclusion][23] * [Policies and positions][24] * [Suppliers][25] * [Suppliers overview][26] * [Supplier registration][27] * [Supplier help for Ariba][28] * [Research][29] * [Research overview][30] * [Areas of focus][31] * [Oncology][32] * [Vaccines][33] * [Infectious diseases][34] * [Cardiometabolic and respiratory diseases ][35] * [Immunology][36] * [Neuroscience][37] * [Ophthalmology][38] * [Areas of innovation][39] * [Data science and artificial intelligence ][40] * [Green and sustainable science][41] * [Our therapeutic modalities][42] * [Translational medicine][43] * [Pipeline][44] * [Business development and licensing (BD&L)][45] * [Clinical trials][46] * [Clinical trials overview][47] * [Find a trial][48] * [Diversity in clinical trials][49] * [R&D locations][50] * [How we invent][51] * [Meet our scientists][52] * [Publications][53] * [Products][54] * [Products list][55] * [Safety data sheets][56] * [Merck authorized distributors][57] * [Patients][58] * [Patients overview][59] * [Patient support programs][60] * [Play an active role in your health care][61] * [Fighting counterfeit medicine][62] * [Investors][63] * [Investors overview][64] * [Events & presentations][65] * [Financial information][66] * [Financial information overview][67] * [SEC filings][68] * [Stock information][69] * [Investor resources][70] * [Media][71] * [Media overview][72] * [News releases][73] * [Company statements][74] * [Media library & contacts][75] * [Company fact sheet][76] * [Careers][77] #### Who we are [Learn more][78] [Contact us][79] [Worldwide][80] See our worldwide locations information ## What can we help you find? Search for: [Pause video] [Play video] ## Announcing first positive Phase 3 topline results for our investigational individualized ## neoantigen therapy plus immunotherapy for certain patients with completely resected stage IIB-IV ## melanoma [ Learn more ][81] ### Oncology Our teams of researchers and scientists are pushing the boundaries of cancer research to discover more effective anticancer therapies. ### Investors Find our latest financials, events and presentations, news, stock information and investor contacts. ### Sustainability We operate responsibly every day to enable a safe and healthy future for people and communities globally. ## Explore our stories [ ][82] [ Innovation What are individualized neoantigen therapies? ][83] [ ][84] [ Health awareness Understanding melanoma: The signs and risk factors ][85] [ ][86] [ Innovation How Merck scientists are driving next-generation cancer research ][87] [ ][88] [ Innovation Merck’s One Pipeline strategy: Purpose, patients and big bets on science ][89] 1 [Read more stories][90] ### About us For more than 130 years, we have brought hope to humanity through the development of important medicines and vaccines. [Who we are][91] [What we do][92] × ### Pipeline We follow the science where we can make the greatest difference, now and in the future. [Explore our pipeline][93] × ### Clinical trials Clinical trials help find new treatments to help save and improve lives. Our progress is due in large part to the important and tough scientific questions we set out to answer with our trials and collaborations. [Learn more about clinical trials][94] × ## Related links [ **Media** Our latest news, announcements and multimedia resources. ][95] [ **Contact us** If you have a question or need more information about us, find out who you should contact here. ][96] [ **Research** We believe research is the will to conquer the impossible and that science will lead the way. ][97] ### Connect with us on social For patients and health care professionals * [MerckHelps][98] Merck Patient Assistance Program provides certain Merck medicines and adult vaccines for free to qualified patients. * [Merck Access Program][99] Information about insurance coverage and financial assistance options for eligible patients. * [Clinical trials][100] Learn about our clinical trials and find available studies. * [Merck Manuals][101] Medical information source covering thousands of topics in all fields of medicine. Sustainability * [Impact Report][102] Reporting on our commitment to operating responsibly to benefit society. * [Merck for Mothers][103] An initiative to create a world where no woman has to die giving life. About Merck * [Merck Animal Health][104] The global animal health business unit of Merck. * [Health Plan - Transparency in Coverage][105] In compliance with the Consolidated Appropriations Act, learn more about our health plan’s pricing information. * [Contact Us][106] If you have a question or need more information about us, find out who you should contact. * [Forward-looking statement][107] * [Cookie policy][108] * [Cookie Preferences][109] * [Privacy][110] * [Transparency disclosure][111] * [Terms of use][112] * [Accessibility][113] * [Sitemap][114] * [Consumer Health Data Privacy Policy][115] * [Your Privacy Choices ][116] Copyright © 2026 Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA and its affiliates. All rights reserved. | This site is intended only for residents of the United States and Canada. ### Forward-Looking Statement of Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, N.J., USA This website of Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, N.J., USA (the “company”) includes “forward-looking statements” within the meaning of the safe harbor provisions of the U.S. Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995. These statements are based upon the current beliefs and expectations of the company’s management and are subject to significant risks and uncertainties. There can be no guarantees with respect to pipeline candidates that the candidates will receive the necessary regulatory approvals or that they will prove to be commercially successful. If underlying assumptions prove inaccurate or risks or uncertainties materialize, actual results may differ materially from those set forth in the forward-looking statements. Risks and uncertainties include but are not limited to, general industry conditions and competition; general economic factors, including interest rate and currency exchange rate fluctuations; the impact of pharmaceutical industry regulation and health care legislation in the United States and internationally; global trends toward health care cost containment; technological advances, new products and patents attained by competitors; challenges inherent in new product development, including obtaining regulatory approval; the company’s ability to accurately predict future market conditions; manufacturing difficulties or delays; financial instability of international economies and sovereign risk; dependence on the effectiveness of the company’s patents and other protections for innovative products; and the exposure to litigation, including patent litigation, and/or regulatory actions. The company undertakes no obligation to publicly update any forward-looking statement, whether as a result of new information, future events or otherwise. Additional factors that could cause results to differ materially from those described in the forward-looking statements can be found in the company’s Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2025 and the company’s other filings with the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) available at the SEC’s Internet site ([www.sec.gov][117]). **No Duty to Update** The information contained in this website was current as of the date presented. The company assumes no duty to update the information to reflect subsequent developments. Consequently, the company will not update the information contained in the website and investors should not rely upon the information as current or accurate after the presentation date. [Decline][118] [Accept][119] [1]: #content [2]: https://www.merck.com/ [3]: # [4]: https://www.merck.com/company-overview/ [5]: https://www.merck.com/company-overview/ [6]: https://www.merck.com/what-we-do/ [7]: https://www.merck.com/stories/ [8]: https://www.merck.com/company-overview/history/ [9]: https://www.merck.com/company-overview/sustainability/ [10]: https://www.merck.com/company-overview/sustainability/ [11]: https://www.merck.com/company-overview/sustainability/philanthropy/ [12]: https://www.merck.com/company-ove