[Partnering with patient organisations][26]\n  * [Partnering with members of the public][27]\n  * [Grants and Donations][28]\n* [Stories][29]\n* [Careers][30]\n\nWorldwide\n\n# Welcome to Roche UK\n\n##### Ukraine Support Hotline & Contact Information\n\nPlease visit [roche.ua][31] for dedicated support hotline contacts and medical information.\n\n[A woman with dark hair, wearing a mustard yellow blazer and white shirt, speaking in front of a\nplain gray background, with caption: 'At Roche UK, we believe time is precious.]\n\n## About Roche in the UK\n\nFor well over a century, we’ve focused our energy and investment in developing tests and treatments\nthat change lives and give people more quality time with the people they love.\n\n[\nRead more\n][32]\n\n## Partnerships\n\nOnly by partnering with the brightest minds in science and healthcare, can we serve patients with\ndifficult-to-treat diseases, both now and in the future.\n\n[\nRead more\n][33]\n\n## Find clinical trials and observational studies\n\nFor information on clinical trials, click \"read more\" to visit clinicaltrials.gov, or visit\nhttps://eudract.ema.europa.eu/.\n\n[\nRead more\n][34]\n\n## Recent stories from\n## Roche UK\n\n### [Navigating Multiple Sclerosis Together][35]\n\nNavigating a new diagnosis of multiple sclerosis (MS) can feel overwhelming, but patients do not\nhave to walk this path alone.\n\n18 May 2026\n\n### [Raising the bar in haemophilia A care][36]\n\nNeeds evolve, and so must care. The future of haemophilia A care demands bold innovation,\npersonalised solutions, and an unwavering commitment to the evolving needs of people affected by\nthis condition.\n\n16 April 2026\n[A nurse in blue scrubs checks an elderly patient's blood pressure with a stethoscope, conveying\ncare and professionalism in a home setting.]\n\n### [Hypertension: What can be done to change the trajectory and improve patient care? ][37]\n\nUnderstanding the causes and tackling the challenge of the world’s leading preventable cause of\ncardiovascular diseases\n\n22 July 2025\n\n## For professionals\n\n### [Careers][38]\n\nWe strive to attract and retain the best people by maintaining a culture where old ideas can be\nchallenged, new ideas can flourish and we can all learn from each other.\n\nM-GB-00026548\n\nDate of Preparation June 2026\n* [Contact][39]\n* [Locations][40]\n\n### Helpful links\n* [ Our medicines][41]\n* [Our role in pharma][42]\n* [Our role in testing & diagnostics][43]\n* [Roche careers][44]\n* [Stories][45]\n* [Privacy policy ][46]\n* [Terms & Conditions][47]\n* Cookies\n* [Modern Slavery Act][48]\n* [Accessibility Statement][49]\n\n©  F. Hoffmann-La Roche Ltd  \n\nThis website contains information which is intended for a UK audience only.\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: /\n[3]: https://careers.roche.com/global/en\n[4]: /search\n[5]: /search\n[6]: /about\n[7]: /about/business\n[8]: /about/governance\n[9]: /about/sustainability\n[10]: /partnerships\n[11]: /partnerships/partnering-with-industry\n[12]: /partnerships/collaborative-working-with-the-nhs\n[13]: /partnerships/partnering-with-healthcare-professionals\n[14]: /partnerships/working-with-patient-organisations\n[15]: /partnerships/partnering-with-members-of-the-public\n[16]: /partnerships/grants-and-donations\n[17]: /stories\n[18]: /about\n[19]: /about/business\n[20]: /about/governance\n[21]: /about/sustainability\n[22]: "}}, "page_text": "[Skip to main content][1] [][2] * [Careers][3] [][4] [][5] * About Roche * [About Roche][6] * [Business][7] * [Governance][8] * [Sustainability][9] * Partnerships * [Partnerships][10] * [Partnering with industry][11] * [Partnering with the NHS][12] * [Partnering with healthcare professionals][13] * [Partnering with patient organisations][14] * [Partnering with members of the public][15] * [Grants and Donations][16] * [Stories][17] * About Roche * [About Roche][18] * [Business][19] * [Governance][20] * [Sustainability][21] * Partnerships * [Partnerships][22] * [Partnering with industry][23] * [Partnering with the NHS][24] * [Partnering with healthcare professionals][25] * [Partnering with patient organisations][26] * [Partnering with members of the public][27] * [Grants and Donations][28] * [Stories][29] * [Careers][30] Worldwide # Welcome to Roche UK ##### Ukraine Support Hotline & Contact Information Please visit [roche.ua][31] for dedicated support hotline contacts and medical information. [A woman with dark hair, wearing a mustard yellow blazer and white shirt, speaking in front of a plain gray background, with caption: 'At Roche UK, we believe time is precious.] ## About Roche in the UK For well over a century, we’ve focused our energy and investment in developing tests and treatments that change lives and give people more quality time with the people they love. [ Read more ][32] ## Partnerships Only by partnering with the brightest minds in science and healthcare, can we serve patients with difficult-to-treat diseases, both now and in the future. [ Read more ][33] ## Find clinical trials and observational studies For information on clinical trials, click \"read more\" to visit clinicaltrials.gov, or visit https://eudract.ema.europa.eu/. [ Read more ][34] ## Recent stories from ## Roche UK ### [Navigating Multiple Sclerosis Together][35] Navigating a new diagnosis of multiple sclerosis (MS) can feel overwhelming, but patients do not have to walk this path alone. 18 May 2026 ### [Raising the bar in haemophilia A care][36] Needs evolve, and so must care. The future of haemophilia A care demands bold innovation, personalised solutions, and an unwavering commitment to the evolving needs of people affected by this condition. 16 April 2026 [A nurse in blue scrubs checks an elderly patient's blood pressure with a stethoscope, conveying care and professionalism in a home setting.] ### [Hypertension: What can be done to change the trajectory and improve patient care? ][37] Understanding the causes and tackling the challenge of the world’s leading preventable cause of cardiovascular diseases 22 July 2025 ## For professionals ### [Careers][38] We strive to attract and retain the best people by maintaining a culture where old ideas can be challenged, new ideas can flourish and we can all learn from each other. M-GB-00026548 Date of Preparation June 2026 * [Contact][39] * [Locations][40] ### Helpful links * [ Our medicines][41] * [Our role in pharma][42] * [Our role in testing & diagnostics][43] * [Roche careers][44] * [Stories][45] * [Privacy policy ][46] * [Terms & Conditions][47] * Cookies * [Modern Slavery Act][48] * [Accessibility Statement][49] © F. Hoffmann-La Roche Ltd This website contains information which is intended for a UK audience only. [1]: #main-content [2]: / [3]: https://careers.roche.com/global/en [4]: /search [5]: /search [6]: /about [7]: /about/business [8]: /about/governance [9]: /about/sustainability [10]: /partnerships [11]: /partnerships/partnering-with-industry [12]: /partnerships/collaborative-working-with-the-nhs [13]: /partnerships/partnering-with-healthcare-professionals [14]: /partnerships/working-with-patient-organisations [15]: /partnerships/partnering-with-members-of-the-public [16]: /partnerships/grants-and-donations [17]: /stories [18]: /about [19]: /about/business [20]: /about/governance [21]: /about/sustainability [22]: /partnerships [23]: /partnerships/partnering-with-industry [24]: /partnerships/collaborative-working-with-the-nhs [25]: /partnerships/partnering-with-healthcare-professionals [26]: /partnerships/working-with-patient-organisations [27]: /partnerships/partnering-with-members-of-the-public [28]: /partnerships/grants-and-donations [29]: /stories [30]: https://careers.roche.com/global/en [31]: https://www.roche.ua/ [32]: /about/ [33]: /partnerships/ [34]: https://clinicaltrials.gov/ [35]: /stories/navigating-multiple-sclerosis-together [36]: /stories/raising-the-bar-in-haemophilia-a-care [37]: /stories/improving-hypertension-care [38]: https://careers.r