ld monitor integration progress and expanded manufacturing network. The sustained Dow Jones sustainability listing reinforces ESG credibility. The homepage counters (capacity, approvals, batch success rate, global clients) were not visible in the static content, so quantitative performance metrics should be sourced from financial reports or IR pages."}, "location": {"offices": ["300, Songdo bio-daero, Yeonsu-gu, Incheon, Republic of Korea", "Bio Campus I", "Bio Campus II", "Rockville Campus"], "countries": ["South Korea", "United States"], "regions_served": ["Global"]}, "media": {"articles": [], "press_releases": [], "investor_presentations": []}}, "page_text": "Samsung Biologics is expanding its global CDMO footprint through the announced all-cash acquisition of PolyPeptide Group AG, which strengthens its multi-modality strategy and adds capacity in the U.S., Europe, and India. The company emphasizes end-to-end services from research to commercial manufacturing, with strong capabilities in biologics, bioconjugation, mRNA, and advanced modalities.", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "Samsung Biologics — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: CDMO manufacturing biosimilars for clients; may not market own brand but builds products. | Major CDMO in Asia Pacific, manufacturing biosimilars for global clients. | South Korea | Incheon, South Korea", "role_description": "Marketer"}}, "X Score": "63", "Y Score": "66", "Overall Score": "64", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Biotechnology", "Quadrant": "Leaders"}, {"Company": "Sandoz", "Website": "https://www.sandoz.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "Basel, Switzerland, Its", "Continent / Geography": "EU(Switzerland)", "Operational Presence": "Switzerland", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Global leader in biosimilars, a Novartis division", "Key Brands Repre