ectors/ [34]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/corporate-governance/management/ [35]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/corporate-governance/remuneration/ [36]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/corporate-governance/auditors/ [37]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/corporate-governance/articles-of-association/ [38]: https://xbrane.careers.haileyhr.app/ [39]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/contact/ [40]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/about-xbrane/ [41]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/investors-media/ [42]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/about-xbrane/ [43]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/science-and-technology/ [44]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/portfolio/ [45]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/investors-media/presentations-and-in-media/ [46]: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1183360100 [47]: https://www.redeye.se/video/event-presentation/1142723/xbrane-biopharma-ceo-martin-amark-prese nts-at-redeye-life-science-day-2025-december-3 [48]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/investors-media/press-releases/ [49]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/xbrane-biopharma-releases-interim-report-for-january-june-2026/ [50]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/xbrane-biopharma-ab-and-joinn-biologics-us-inc-enter-strategic-partn ership-to-develop-xdarzane-xbranes-biosimilar-candidate-to-darzalex-daratumumab/ [51]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/xbrane-biopharma-ab-publ-xbrane-or-the-company-nasdaq-stockholm-xbra ne-receives-fda-bsufa-date-of-october-29-2026-for-its-investigational-biosimilar-candida/ [52]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/announcement-from-the-annual-general-meeting-in-xbrane-biopharma-ab/ [53]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/xbrane-biopharma-abs-publ-xbrane-interim-report-january-march-2026-i s-as-of-today-available-on-the-companys-website-www-xbrane-com/ [54]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/about-xbrane/ [55]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/science-and-technology/ [56]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/portfolio/ [57]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/investors-media/ [58]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/about-xbrane/ [59]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/science-and-technology/ [60]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/portfolio/ [61]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/investors-media/ [62]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/corporate-governance/ [63]: https://xbrane.careers.haileyhr.app/ [64]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/contact/ [65]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/whistleblower/ [66]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/privacy-policy/ [67]: https://www.xbrane.com/en/cookie-policy/ [68]: /cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#bad3d4dcd5fac2d8c8dbd4df94d9d5d7 [69]: #", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "Xbrane Biopharma AB — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Develops biosimilars, a key segment of biologics market. | Xbrane is a Swedish biopharmaceutical company developing biosimilars, with a presence in the German market. | Sweden | Stockholm, Sweden", "role_description": "Brand"}}, "X Score": "60", "Y Score": "50", "Overall Score": "55", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Biotechnology", "Quadrant": "Trailblazers"}, {"Company": "Zai Lab", "Website": "https://www.zailaboratory.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "Shanghai, China", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(China)", "Operational Presence": "China", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Markets biologics in China, including niraparib and other oncology products.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Marketer", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Marketer", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "CN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Zai Lab — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Markets biologics in China, including oncology products.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "85", "X Score": "41", "Y Score": "51", "Overall Score": "46", "Industry Category": "Healthcare / Biotechnology", "Quadrant": "Emerging Players"}, {"Company": "Zydus Lifesciences", "Website": "https://www.zyduslife.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "Ahmedabad, Gujarat, India", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(India)", "Operational Presence": "India", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Zydus develops and markets biosimilars and biologics.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "Brand", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "IN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Zydus Lifesciences — channel participant (chatgpt_recall). Verify: Zydus is a pharmaceutical company that develops and markets biosimilars and biologics, owning and marketing its products.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Brand", "verify_confidence": "90", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "zyduslife.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "zyduslife.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "[[Zydus Lifesciences]][1] [[Zydus Logo]][2]\n* [Home][3]\n* [The Company][4]\n* [Operations][5]\n* [Research][6]\n* [Products][7]\n* [News Updates][8]\n* [Investor Zone][9]\n* [Careers][10]\n* [Media Kit][11]\n* [Contact us][12]\nSubscribe to our Newsletter ×\n[Pharmaceutical Solutions]\n\n# A legacy of 70 years in bringing innovative pharmaceutical solutions to life\n\n[About us][13]\n[Innovation Excellence]\n\n## Driven by a passion for innovation, making a difference in the world of health and care\n\n[Innovation Excellence][14]\n[Zydus Srishti]\n\n# Living our mission of creating healthier, happier communities globally\n\n[Zydus Srishti][15]\n\n## Over 29000 people impacting lives across the world\n\nZydus group is headquartered in Ahmedabad, India, and ranks 4th in the Indian pharmaceutical\nindustry. The group has manufacturing sites and research facilities spread across five states of\nGujarat, Maharashtra, Goa, Himachal Pradesh and Sikkim in India and in the US and Brazil.\n\nZydus’ global business has a strong presence in the regulated markets of the US, Europe (France and\nSpain) and in the high profile markets of Latin America and South Africa. It is also present in a\nbig way in 25 other emerging markets worldwide.\n* [Business Sites][16]\n* [Mfg. Sites][17]\n* [R & D Sites][18]\n* [Joint Venture][19]\n\n[Map]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map]\n[Map Pointer]\n[Map Pointer]\n\n## Where Innovation Shapes Healthcare Solutions\n\n**Zydus’ Innovation programme** is spearheaded by **1500 researchers** across 19 sites, working on\ndifferentiated medicines for the future.\nFrom NCEs to vaccines, biosimilars and niche technologies, the group is exploring\ndifferent ideas and concepts, innovating constantly.\n\n## Major Areas of Research\n\n[NCE Research] **NCE Research**\n* Cardio-Metabolic\n* Inflammation and Immunology,\n* Neurosciences, Oncology, Rare Diseases\n[Biologics] **Biologics**\n* Biosimilar Therapeutic proteins\n* Biosimilar Monoclonal antibodies\n* Biobetters and Novel biologics\n[Vaccines] **Vaccines**\n* Infectious diseases\n[View More][20]\n\n## Innovation that bridges unmet healthcare needs.\n\n[[Tablets]][21]\n[\n\n#### Twinrab^{TM} : A Breakthrough innovation in rabies PEP\n\nWorld’s First Novel Rabies Monoclonal Antibodies (mAbs) cocktail containing Docaravimab and\nMiromavimab, providing dual protection against rabies.\n\n][22]\n[Saroglitazar Tablets]\n\n#### Lipaglyn - Novel drug to treat diabetic dyslipidemia, a global, unmet healthcare need.\n\nThe first NCE from an Indian research pipeline to move from the lab to the market.\n\n[Adalimumab]\n\n#### [Exemptia - The world’s first biosimilar of Adalimumab, the largest selling therapy globally\n#### for treating auto immune disorders.][23]\n\nProvides a new lease of life to Indian patients of inflammatory arthritis, who did not have access\nto this revolutionary therapy, so far.\n\n[VaxiFlu-4]\n\n#### Vaxiflu-4 - India’s 1st Tetravalent Inactivated Influenza vaccine.\n\nThe vaccine provides protection from the four influenza viruses- H1N1, H3N2, Type B (Brisbane) and\nType B (Phuket).\n\n## State-of-the-art manufacturing capabilities.\n\n[Manufacturing]\n\nAs one of the key players amongst the pharmaceutical manufacturing companies, the group has\nmanufacturing capabilities across the entire pharmaceutical value chain: including formulations,\nAPIs, vaccines, biosimilars, complex products (transdermals, topical etc.), animal health products\nand wellness products. It has more than 30 manufacturing plants worldwide including India, Brazil\nand USA.\n\n[View More][24]\n\n\n## Latest updates\n\n[Zydus and Beihai Biotech sign an exclusive licensing, supply and commerciali"}}, "page_text": "[[Zydus Lifesciences]][1] [[Zydus Logo]][2] * [Home][3] * [The Company][4] * [Operations][5] * [Research][6] * [Products][7] * [News Updates][8] * [Investor Zone][9] * [Careers][10] * [Media Kit][11] * [Contact us][12] Subscribe to our Newsletter × [Pharmaceutical Solutions] # A legacy of 70 years in bringing innovative pharmaceutical solutions to life [About us][13] [Innovation Excellence] ## Driven by a passion for innovation, making a difference in the world of health and care [Innovation Excellence][14] [Zydus Srishti] # Living our mission of creating healthier, happier communities globally [Zydus Srishti][15] ## Over 29000 people impacting lives across the world Zydus group is headquartered in Ahmedabad, India, and ranks 4th in the Indian pharmaceutical industry. The group has manufacturing sites and research facilities spread across five states of Gujarat, Maharashtra, Goa, Himachal Pradesh and Sikkim in India and in the US and Brazil. Zydus’ global business has a strong presence in the regulated markets of the US, Europe (France and Spain) and in the high profile markets of Latin America and South Africa. It is also present in a big way in 25 other emerging markets worldwide. * [Business Sites][16] * [Mfg. Sites][17] * [R & D Sites][18] * [Joint Venture][19] [Map] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] [Map] [Map Pointer] [Map Pointer] ## Where Innovation Shapes Healthcare Solutions **Zydus’ Innovation programme** is spearheaded by **1500 researchers** across 19 sites, working on differentiated medicines for the future. From NCEs to vaccines, biosimilars and niche technologies, the group is exploring different ideas and concepts, innovating constantly. ## Major Areas of Research [NCE Research] **NCE Research** * Cardio-Metabolic * Inflammation and Immunology, * Neurosciences, Oncology, Rare Diseases [Biologics] **Biologics** * Biosimilar Therapeutic proteins * Biosimilar Monoclonal antibodies * Biobetters and Novel biologics [Vaccines] **Vaccines** * Infectious diseases [View More][20] ## Innovation that bridges unmet healthcare needs. [[Tablets]][21] [ #### Twinrab^{TM} : A Breakthrough innovation in rabies PEP World’s First Novel Rabies Monoclonal Antibodies (mAbs) cocktail containing Docaravimab and Miromavimab, providing dual protection against rabies. ][22] [Saroglitazar Tablets] #### Lipaglyn - Novel drug to treat diabetic dyslipidemia, a global, unmet healthcare need. The first NCE from an Indian research pipeline to move from the lab to the market. [Adalimumab] #### [Exemptia - The world’s first biosimilar of Adalimumab, the largest selling therapy globally #### for treating auto immune disorders.][23] Provides a new lease of life to Indian patients of inflammatory arthritis, who did not have access to this revolutionary therapy, so far. [VaxiFlu-4] #### Vaxiflu-4 - India’s 1st Tetravalent Inactivated Influenza vaccine. The vaccine provides protection from the four influenza viruses- H1N1, H3N2, Type B (Brisbane) and Type B (Phuket). ## State-of-the-art manufacturing capabilities. [Manufacturing] As one of the key players amongst the pharmaceutical manufacturing companies, the group has manufacturing capabilities across the entire pharmaceutical value chain: including formulations, APIs, vaccines, biosimilars, complex products (transdermals, topical etc.), animal health products and wellness products. It has more than 30 manufacturing plants worldwide including India, Brazil and USA. [View More][24] ## Latest updates [Zydus and Beihai Biotech sign an exclusive licensing, supply and commercialization agreement for BEIZRAY (Albumin Solubilized Docetaxel Injection), a 505(B)(2) product for the US market][25] Posted on: 14 Feb 2025 [Intimation of ESG Rating][26] Posted on: 06 Feb 2025 [Zydus Lifesciences Limited Financial Performance for Q3 FY25 Revenue from operations at Rs. 52,691 mn, up 17% YoY Net Profit at Rs. 10,235 mn, up 30% YoY][27] Posted on: 05 Feb 2025 [Press Release][28] Posted on: 05 Feb 2025 [Celebrating the Legacy of Excellence and Innovation Zydus Takeda Healthcare marks 25 years of manufacturing operations in India][29] Posted on: 30 Jan 2025 [Mr. Pankaj R. Patel, Chairman, Zydus Lifesciences Limited conferred with Padma Bhushan][30] Posted on: 26 Jan 2025 [Order-In-Original from Office of Assistant Commissioner, CGST Division, Baddi, Himachal Pradesh][31] Posted on: 25 Jan 2025 [View More][32] Social media updates [[Linkdin]][33] [[twitter]][34] [[twitter]][35] [[twitter]][36] [[twitter]][37] ### / @ZydusUniverse [ The Company ][38] * [The Brand][39] * [Mission][40] * [Community][41] * [ESG Report 2021-22][42] * [ESG Report 2022-23][43] * [ESG Report FY-2023-24][44] * [ESG Report FY-2024-25][45] * [BRSR FY23 Mapped with Global ESG Frameworks][46] * [Impact Assessment Report][47] * [Awards][48] * [Privacy Policy][49] * [MRP Change][50] * [Podcast][51] * [CSR Projects][52] [ Operations ][53] * [India Business][54] * [Global Presence][55] * [Manufacturing][56] * [EHS Policy][57] [ Research ][58] * [Focus][59] * [New Chemical Entities][60] * [Biologics][61] * [Vaccines][62] * [Research Pipeline][63] * [Scientific Activities][64] * [Collaborate][65] * [Zydus Therapeutics][66] [ Products ][67] * [India Formulations][68] * [Generics][69] * [ Zydus Biologics][70] * [ International][71] [ Investor Zone ][72] * [Board Of Directors][73] * [Composition Of Committees][74] * [Scheme][75] * [Financials][76] * [Investor Presentation][77] * [Teleconferences][78] * [AGM][79] * [Share Holder Service][80] * [Buy Back 2022][81] * [Buy Back 2024][82] * [Buy Back 2026][83] * [Share Holding Pattern][84] * [Policies][85] * [Disclosures under Regulation 46 of Listing Regulation][86] * [Smartodr][87] [ News Updates ][88] * [Press Releases][89] [ Careers ][90] Warning Regarding Fraudulent Job Postings: Authenticate your job offer letter [ India ][91] [ USA ][92] [ Media Kit ][93] [ Contact Us ][94] [Adverse Event Reporting][95] [Vendor Registration Portal][96] [RFQ/AUCTION EVENT PARTICIPATION TRAINING GUIDE][97] [close] [ZydusLife] Copyright © 2026 Zydus Group. All Rights Reserved. “By continuing to browse this site, you are consenting to the use of cookies for providing you optimum site performance, best 